# Matrix Client Patterns

## Client Lifecycle

- Created in `matrix/client.rs` via `create_matrix_client`
- Logs in with username/password from environment variables
- Background sync loop runs via `start_background_sync` with backoff on errors
- Client is shared across all tool invocations (not ephemeral per-request)

## Client Cache (`matrix/cache.rs`)

- Keyed by `userId:homeserverUrl`
- 15-minute TTL with periodic cleanup task
- Primed for multi-identity scenarios
- `shutdownAllClients()` equivalent on process signals

## Background Sync

- Loops `sync_once` to keep room state fresh
- Implements exponential backoff on sync errors
- Essential for tools that read room state, messages, and members

## SKIP_MATRIX_INIT Mode

When `SKIP_MATRIX_INIT=true`:
- Builds a stub client, skips real sync/cache wiring
- MCP protocol works normally
- Tool calls will hit connection/state errors
- Used for MCP Inspector and protocol-only testing

## Important Notes

- Config includes OAuth/token exchange env vars but auth is minimal (planned, not implemented)
- `rejectUnauthorized: false` equivalent for local dev TLS -- not production-safe
- matrix-sdk 0.10 with rustls -- no OpenSSL dependency
